// WHERE A SHIP'S LADDER PUTS YOU. Keyed on the ladder's own coord, which includes its floor, so one
// table covers both directions: the up ladder at 3609,3543 is on L0 and the down ladder on the same
// two numbers is on L1, and they are different rows here.
//
// Every arrival tile below was checked walkable on the destination floor (tools/sim/questprobe.ts
// and a sweep of the decks). That is the whole point of the table - the handler used to mirror the
// player through the loc, and on the wreck's aft ladder that mirror lands you inside the hull.
[ahoy_ladder_landing]
inputtype=coord
outputtype=coord
default=null
// --- the wreck, west of Port Phasmatys: hold (L0), deck (L1), quarterdeck (L2)
val=0_56_55_25_23,1_56_55_24_23   // 3609,3543 up   -> 3608,3543
val=0_56_55_29_23,1_56_55_30_23   // 3613,3543 up   -> 3614,3543, beside the deck door
val=1_56_55_31_21,2_56_55_32_21   // 3615,3541 up   -> 3616,3541
val=1_56_55_31_25,2_56_55_32_25   // 3615,3545 up   -> 3616,3545
val=1_56_55_25_23,0_56_55_26_23   // 3609,3543 down -> 3610,3543
val=1_56_55_29_23,0_56_55_28_23   // 3613,3543 down -> 3612,3543
val=2_56_55_31_21,1_56_55_30_21   // 3615,3541 down -> 3614,3541
val=2_56_55_31_25,1_56_55_32_25   // 3615,3545 down -> 3616,3545, NOT 3614,3545 which is hull
// --- the ghost ship at the Port Phasmatys pier
val=0_57_54_48_55,1_57_54_48_56   // 3696,3511 up   -> 3696,3512
val=0_57_54_48_60,1_57_54_48_59   // 3696,3516 up   -> 3696,3515
val=1_57_54_48_55,0_57_54_48_54   // 3696,3511 down -> 3696,3510
val=1_57_54_48_60,0_57_54_48_61   // 3696,3516 down -> 3696,3517
// --- the ghost ship's ANGLED pair, pier side, linking the deck (L1) to the quarterdeck (L2).
// Two placements, each with a partner directly above it, at 3694,3510 and 3698,3510. The four rows
// here were DERIVED, not measured, and that is the one place on these two ships where that is true.
// The reason is worth writing down so nobody mistakes these numbers for the others:
//
// EVERY TILE ON DECKS 1 AND 2 OF THIS SHIP READS WALKABLE. There is no collision data up there at
// all - a 17x13 sweep of both floors comes back open but for the ladder locs themselves. So the
// check that makes the rest of this table trustworthy, "is the arrival tile standable", cannot fail
// on these four rows and cannot be used to choose between candidates. Neither can ahoyladders.ts,
// which is why its new rows prove only that the ladders answer and move you.
//
// GIVEN THAT, THE OFFSET COMES FROM THE MODEL. These two locs are shipladder_angled and
// shipladder_top_angled, whose own handler in ladders+stairs/scripts/ladders.rs2 steps TWO TILES OUT
// in the direction the ladder faces - an angled ladder leans, and you arrive at the top of the lean.
// Both lower locs face angle 2 and both upper ones angle 0, so up goes south and down goes north.
//
// WHY THE TABLE ANYWAY, when the offset is arithmetic. Because arithmetic is what put a player
// inside this hull once already. A wrong number here is a one-line edit to a documented value that
// ahoyladders.ts then re-checks; a wrong rule in the handler is a bug on twelve other placements.
val=1_57_54_50_54,2_57_54_50_52   // 3698,3510 up   -> 3698,3508, derived
val=1_57_54_46_54,2_57_54_46_52   // 3694,3510 up   -> 3694,3508, derived
val=2_57_54_50_54,1_57_54_50_56   // 3698,3510 down -> 3698,3512, derived
val=2_57_54_46_54,1_57_54_46_56   // 3694,3510 down -> 3694,3512, derived
